==========================================================================
I. COUPLING TO CPU-SIDE DEQUANT (exp20 dependency)
==========================================================================
Raising aggregate BW only helps while VQ3R dequant keeps up. At
aggregate B GiB/s the dequant loop must sustain B GiB/s of 3-bit-index
-> dim-8 codeword expansion. exp20 is measuring exactly that ceiling.
If dequant sustains D GiB/s aggregate, usable BW = min(B, D).
  1x 990 Pro (BASELINE, measured)    needs dequant >=   5.92 GiB/s
  2x 990 Pro duplicate               needs dequant >=  11.84 GiB/s
  2x 990 Pro sharded (uniform hash)  needs dequant >=   9.90 GiB/s
  3x 990 Pro duplicate               needs dequant >=  15.78 GiB/s
  3x 990 Pro sharded                 needs dequant >=  12.91 GiB/s
  4x 990 Pro duplicate (bifurc)      needs dequant >=  23.68 GiB/s
  4x 990 Pro sharded (bifurc)        needs dequant >=  15.43 GiB/s
  2x 9100 Pro Gen5 duplicate         needs dequant >=  23.52 GiB/s
  4x 9100 Pro Gen5 duplicate         needs dequant >=  47.04 GiB/s
  4x 9100 Pro Gen5 sharded           needs dequant >=  30.65 GiB/s

